1
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,680
I’m pretty good at sex, you know.

2
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,320
You literally just found that out last night

3
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:10,320
Who

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:11,440
From now on,

5
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,040
we’ll be nothing more than boss and subordinate

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,320
Yok’s job is to learn as an intern,

7
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:15,400
and my job is to teach Yok.

8
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:16,480
OK？

9
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,720
Are you and Yok going to Pattaya together

10
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:19,680
Can I come with you, too?

11
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:20,680
We’re not going there for fun.

12
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,000
It’s enough that you’re going with Yok.

13
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,160
Itt

14
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:29,400
Want some?

15
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,600
I thought you said we were going to talk about work.

16
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,960
Then what was that at the beach?

17
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,280
I’ll make you get over me.

18
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:36,000
You really think someone like you can pull that off.

19
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:46,760
Dammit, why do we have to take the fire escape?

20
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,720
And you went so hard on me last night.

21
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:49,840
How am I supposed to walk down?

22
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,480
Taking the elevator is too risky.

23
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:52,480
Risky how?

24
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:53,720
Nobody's gonna notice me in this outfit.

25
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,040
No one's going to care.

26
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,600
P'Ing, can you just stop complaining?

27
00:00:58,640 --> 00:00:59,440
Dammit.

28
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,239
How many floors are there?

29
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:05,160
Let me help.

30
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,240
No way.

31
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:08,240
What if you suddenly shove me down the stairs?

32
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:09,520
I don't trust you.

33
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:13,280
Hurry up, P'Ing.

34
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:15,880
Yok, I'm in pain here.

35
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:17,760
Ow, you little...

36
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:34,760
I really don't get it.

37
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,200
Why do we have to book a hotel now that we're back?

38
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,320
Isn't this a bit overkill?

39
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:42,680
Your room is over there.

40
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:43,880
I'm leaving.

41
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,360
Hold on.

42
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,960
Aren't you afraid your family will find out?

43
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,320
Here, just put this on.

44
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:50,920
I don't need one of these

45
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,920
because this limited-edition face of mine

46
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:54,480
is meant to be seen by everyone.

47
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:55,760
Go on.

48
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:57,160
I'm really leaving now.

49
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,160
Hey.

50
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,040
Take your bag with you.

51
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:05,760
You actually look pretty good with those.

52
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:14,360
[Ing: Are you back at the hotel yet?]

53
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,320
[Ing: You're still alive, right?]

54
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,120
[Ing: Voice message]

55
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,360
Why isn't he answering?

56
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:21,000
Is he dead or something?

57
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:23,400
Go away.

58
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,040
What are you doing?

59
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,160
I don't feel anything for P'Ing.

60
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,320
I know I have no right to say this...

61
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,000
I need to check your pocket.

62
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,040
Or do you want me to call the police?

63
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,000
But there's this one person...

64
00:04:34,159 --> 00:04:35,000
who's so talented.

65
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:39,360
He's someone I could never catch up to...

66
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,040
Yes, P'Ing?

67
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:01,160
So you're not dead yet?

68
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:05,880
I'm in my room.

69
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:07,920
Yesterday...

70
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,440
I had quite a bit to drink.

71
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,680
Were you drinking with Yok?

72
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,760
Do you like Yok?

73
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,320
You know what kind of person I am.

74
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,680
Can you just stay out of this?

75
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,400
But he doesn't like you.

76
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:34,320
And his family will never accept you.

77
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:37,159
Just mind your own business, will you?

78
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,680
Does that mean...

79
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,600
you're not serious about him?

80
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,400
Stop meddling and stop asking

81
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,480
so many questions.

82
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:47,000
I'm sorry.

83
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,800
Please don't be mad at me.

84
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:51,200
Your voice is completely hoarse.

85
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,600
Make sure you drink lots of water.

86
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:54,200
When I sent you those messages,

87
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,400
why didn't you reply?

88
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,040
I was just about to,

89
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,320
but you called first.

90
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,600
How could I ever dare to ignore your messages?

91
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:06,560
Whatever. Get yourself sorted out quickly

92
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,560
and get over to the site.

93
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,760
Take plenty of photos to send to Mr. Phet,

94
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,720
understand?

95
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,040
Will do.

96
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,240
And...

97
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:13,840
are you with Yok?

98
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,320
You're asking way too many questions.

99
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,440
Hello?

100
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,160
Hello?

101
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:42,240
Hello?

102
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:46,320
Bring several bottles of your most expensive liquor

103
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:49,040
to room 3102, please.

104
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:50,400
Yes.

105
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,480
Bring everything you've got.

106
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:54,560
I'll finish them all.

107
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:56,320
Bring everything you've got.

108
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:58,840
Thank you.

109
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:01,560
Charge it to the room account.

110
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,360
Thank you.

111
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Think you're so loaded, huh?

112
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,640
I'll help you blow through that money, you jerk.

113
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,040
Oh, you're home?

114
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:25,720
You're not in bed yet, Mom?

115
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:26,360
Not yet.

116
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:29,000
You've only been away for a few days,

117
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,000
but you've got a bit of a tan.

118
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:33,600
What's that mark on your neck?

119
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,200
Just a little accident.

120
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:37,640
That face of yours doesn't just belong to you.

121
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,800
It carries the name of the Sukonsiri family.

122
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,080
It's just a small scratch.

123
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,640
Put some ointment on it, and it'll heal in no time.

124
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:52,120
You'll be fine for Mr. Jomphol's party tomorrow.

125
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,520
No one will even notice it.

126
00:07:54,159 --> 00:07:55,840
A party tomorrow?

127
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,880
It's a welcome party, son.

128
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:02,120
Mr. Jomphol is your dad's business partner from the U.S.

129
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,040
He's moving back to Thailand for good.

130
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:05,720
He has a very talented daughter.

131
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:07,000
She's pretty, too.

132
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,280
Why don't you pick her up tomorrow?

133
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:10,280
I've already prepared a bouquet for you.

134
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,040
I'm sorry.

135
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,560
I'm busy tomorrow.

136
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,360
I have to study for exams.

137
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,680
I can't make it.

138
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,440
You knew you had exams coming up.

139
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:24,160
Why didn't you study ahead of time?

140
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,800
Your internship

141
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:27,360
is affecting your studies, isn't it?

142
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:31,480
Your brother is spoiling you too much.

143
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:36,320
It's okay, son.

144
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:38,640
Put some ointment on it, and it'll heal soon.

145
00:08:38,679 --> 00:08:39,400
Okay.

146
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,400
-If you'll excuse me... -Go on.

147
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:13,800
[Ing: www.xxx.com. Study hard, okay?]

148
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,240
Come in.

149
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,400
You again, Secretary Piang?

150
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:54,320
Unfortunately, it's me again.

151
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:56,520
Were you expecting someone else?

152
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,600
These are the important documents

153
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,120
Mr. Yok sent over.

154
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:05,080
Isn't he supposed to be handling this project?

155
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,560
Yes, but he's currently on leave.

156
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,960
The reason being...

157
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:13,800
severe UV sensitivity.

158
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,200
That's a pathetic excuse.

159
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,560
A whole month off? #VO

160
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,120
What's he even thinking? #VO

161
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:21,560
He literally asked to intern here.

162
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:22,960
Why is he taking so much time off?

163
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:25,360
Should I call him

164
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:27,440
and tell him to work night shifts instead?

165
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:30,160
That way, he avoid the UV rays.

166
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,400
Or should we move his desk

167
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:35,160
to a dark corner somewhere?

168
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:35,760
So there won't be...

169
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,000
Enough, stop talking.

170
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:38,040
Go.

171
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:39,520
Get back to work.

172
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:40,840
Yes, sir.

173
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:50,960
[Ing: Are you coming to the office tomorrow?]

174
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:53,120
[Ing: Hello?]

175
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:57,960
Jeez, my shirt.

176
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,680
Dammit.

177
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:10,800
There's coffee all over it.

178
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,000
Everything is such a mess.

179
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,440
If I want someone...

180
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,440
I don't need to beg you.

181
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,640
You think you're all that?

182
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,840
I can find someone anytime.

183
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:29,680
[Ing: Typing...]

184
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:31,680
[Ing: I'm coming to see you at the shop.]

185
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:35,040
Vince.

186
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,200
Vince.

187
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:40,960
Vince...

188
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,200
Mr. Vince isn't back yet, sir.

189
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:58,320
Then you cut my hair for me.

190
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:18,080
What's your name?

191
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,400
My name is Junior.

192
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:24,160
I've only been here for a month.

193
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,560
If I don't do a very good job,

194
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,520
I'd like to apologize in advance, Mr. Ing.

195
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,080
It's fine. Just get on with it.

196
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:33,880
How old are you?

197
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,080
I'm 21.

198
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:50,840
How long have you been working for Vince?

199
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:51,880
Well...

200
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,160
I've only been here for a month.

201
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:14,080
Hey.

202
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:18,520
Is this really how a CEO's hair should look?

203
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,520
I'm not some rookie in a boy group, you know.

204
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:23,960
Whoa, Ing. Calm down, man.

205
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:26,760
Hey, what are you standing there for?

206
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:27,680
Beat it.

207
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:29,720
Yes, sir.

208
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:31,120
Come on.

209
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,240
Here, just sit down.

210
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:33,440
Stop talking too much.

211
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,640
Look at what happened to my hair.

212
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,120
-Sit down first. -Fix my hair already.

213
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,000
What hairstyle do you want?

214
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:38,040
I'll sort you out myself.

215
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:40,080
Just the usual. Nothing fancy.

216
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:42,120
Don't be so hard on the kid.

217
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,120
He's still new.

218
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,120
You really know how to spot a good one.

219
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:48,960
Junior is a naive one.

220
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,560
Want me to set you up with him?

221
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:53,440
No.

222
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:56,320
I'm off.

223
00:13:58,760 --> 00:13:59,640
No need to see me out.

224
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:01,920
Mr. Ing...

225
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:05,760
I'm really sorry about earlier.

226
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:16,120
Go get yourself a treat.

227
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:47,600
Hello?

228
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:50,520
I'm lost here at your college.

229
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:51,280
Come pick me up.

230
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:52,440
What are you doing here?

231
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,160
I'm busy.

232
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,480
Can't I just come for no reason?

233
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:55,960
It's not like they charge an entrance fee.

234
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:56,800
Bye.

235
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:59,640
Hold on. I'm actually lost,

236
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:00,840
and the mosquitoes here...

237
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,480
are bigger than helicopters.

238
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:04,200
Your phone has data.

239
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:05,840
Just use a map to find your way out.

240
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,480
But the signal is glitching.

241
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:09,480
Why do you think I'm calling you, then?

242
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:11,360
You don't even know where you are.

243
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,800
How am I supposed to know?

244
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:14,640
I'm right next to a big tree.

245
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:17,440
There are hundreds of trees here.

246
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:18,560
Which one are you at?

247
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:20,920
If you're not here to pick me up in ten minutes,

248
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:21,880
I'll call Mr. Phet

249
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,320
and tell him you dumped me after sleeping with me.

250
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:24,160
What?

251
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,720
The clock is ticking.

252
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:26,760
Better hurry up.

253
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,000
What exactly are you doing here?

254
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:03,640
I'm here to see you

255
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,000
and to see that...

256
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,640
you're still hooked on me.

257
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:15,280
I'll ride ahead and guide you to the exit.

258
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,200
What happened isn't going to end that easily.

259
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:33,760
I'm sorry for what I did.

260
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:35,960
I don't lean that way.

261
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,320
I'm begging you.

262
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:38,840
Please don't bring this up again.

263
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,680
Oh, you're sorry?

264
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:41,880
You don't lean that way?

265
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,280
Well, but you already did it.

266
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,640
You still owe me.

267
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:50,720
Are you out of your mind?

268
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:52,760
Yeah, I am.

269
00:16:58,760 --> 00:16:59,440
Let go of me.

270
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,280
Why?

271
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:05,319
What?

272
00:17:17,599 --> 00:17:21,040
Why does your body seem more honest than you are?

273
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:27,400
Follow me.

274
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:30,200
P'Ing...

275
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:42,080
Why are you trying to run away?

276
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:11,520
You didn't mean what you said, did you?

277
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:51,920
I'll be gentle this time. #VO

278
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:52,880
Wait.

279
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:01,880
Why?

280
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,080
You came all this way...

281
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,760
Wasn't it for this?

282
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,440
You still owe me.

283
